What is the chemical composition of Epsom salt, specifically identifying its constituent elements and their proportions?
The chemical composition of Epsom salt is magnesium sulfate (MgSO4), which is an inorganic salt composed of the following elements:

*   Magnesium (Mg)
*   Sulfur (S)
*   Oxygen (O)

The chemical formula for Epsom salt is MgSO4, indicating that one molecule of Epsom salt contains one magnesium ion (Mg2+), one sulfate ion (SO42-), and four oxygen atoms.
